Dragontamer wrote:
> It is easy enough to get 18 strength. But as a human, I'd like to take
> advantage of 18/** strength a human could get. But, it seems nearly
> impossible :-/

It's nice to have that strength but by no way necessary.

> So potions of gain ability only adds one to that counter (that is,
> 18/01 turns into 18/02), spinach and giants are somewhat rare, so
> I obviously can't get them till very late game (late enough that I've
> never actually reached 18/** str yet).
> 
> So are there any other ways to get 18/** strength? Or is it something
> that I won't get every game?

Giants and spinach will give you up to 10 points of strength until
18/90 (further on only 1 point), so those are the primary source of
intrinsic strength. Royal jelly (from bee hives) gives you 1 point
as do blessed potions of gain ability, so these two sources are good
to save until once you reached the 18/90 (but still interesting to
eat them before if you manage to pass beyond some internal limit
that increases your capabilities, or if you have more than 10 units
of this source of strength). If you have a tinning kit it's also
possible to tin the giant zombie corpses; those tins can also give
you the possible maximum of 10 points strength increase. Giants come
often in groups, and they are very nutritious, so lacking a tinning
kit or an amulet of magical breathing will require some other tactics
to get the full strength gain of such a monster group.

